    "body": "In this episode of Denatured, you’ll hear from Jerome Barley, commercial director at Avion Medical and Ryan Klein, vice president, business development, US and APAC at Resolian. We discuss why Australia has become a magnet for early clinical development, and whether its speed, regulatory clarity and tax incentives are pushing it toward a more integrated biotech role.\n> Listen on Spotify > Listen on Apple Podcasts > Listen on Amazon Music > Watch on YouTube\nIn this episode of Denatured, you’ll listen to Jerome Barley, commercial director at Avion Medical and Ryan Klein, vice president, business development, US and APAC at Resolian. We look at why Australia attracts so much early clinical work, and whether its fast timelines, clear rules and tax breaks are turning it into a core player in the biotech industry\nHost\n⁠ Jennifer C. Smith-Parker , Director of Insights, BioSpace\nGuests\nJerome Barley , Commercial Director, Avion Medical\nRyan Klein , Vice President, Business Development, US and APAC, Resolian\nDisclaimer: The views expressed in this discussion by guests are their own and do not represent those of their organizations.",
